  "caveats": [
    "A hit says the WITNESS payload is grouped-era; it does not say the producer is. Re-run the producer to tell a stale artifact from a live source defect. A non-hit is not a clean bill: a witness recording only derived quantities carries no |tr_M| for this to match.",
    "The SOURCE scan reads literals reachable as code, with docstrings excluded (comments never enter an AST). That exclusion is load-bearing, not a convenience: mass_at_3A_proper's docstring quotes both the grouped and the borromean |tr_M| precisely because it EXPLAINS the 2026-09-05 ruling, and flagging it would be flagging the documentation of the fix. Strings are not skipped wholesale, because mp.mpf(\"1.1457...\") is how this corpus writes a high-precision constant.",
    "Fingerprints are computed live, never transcribed, so a re-pin moves them rather than silently invalidating the scan. Only the five atoms at A <= 3 and the two documented pins are covered."
  ],
